WEBVTT

00:00:00.597 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.788 --> 00:00:05.070
In this lesson, we do two things, step by step:

00:00:05.411 --> 00:00:09.870
a refill for a client coming back after a few weeks, and a safe full removal.

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:11.790
Throughout, keep in mind:

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.550
the client's eyes stay closed, and never pull an extension.

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:16.911
Part one:

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:17.871
the refill.

00:00:18.392 --> 00:00:19.151
Step one:

00:00:19.283 --> 00:00:19.951
check in.

00:00:20.275 --> 00:00:22.191
The client sits up with her eyes open.

00:00:22.366 --> 00:00:22.911
Ask:

00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:27.071
after the last appointment, were her eyes red, itchy or swollen?

00:00:27.407 --> 00:00:30.671
Did she lose many lashes or few, did they catch anywhere?

00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:32.591
Look at her eyes in good light.

00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:35.551
If there are signs of a reaction, no refill:

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.111
remove everything instead, as in part two.

00:00:38.779 --> 00:00:39.647
Step two:

00:00:39.886 --> 00:00:40.607
cleanse.

00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:43.647
The client lies down with her eyes closed.

00:00:44.096 --> 00:00:47.419
Wash the lashes with lash cleanser and a soft brush,

00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:50.127
both the extensions and the natural lashes,

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:53.807
because after a few weeks, oil and dust build up at the base.

00:00:54.393 --> 00:00:57.167
Rinse with clean water, then dry thoroughly.

00:00:57.645 --> 00:01:00.724
Then apply the under eye pads, covering the lower lashes,

00:01:00.674 --> 00:01:03.967
without touching the waterline, as in the preparation lesson.

00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:05.408
Step three:

00:01:05.589 --> 00:01:06.688
check every lash.

00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:10.766
Brush the lashes, then glide the straight tweezers lightly through them,

00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:12.288
looking at each lash in turn.

00:01:12.716 --> 00:01:15.846
Look for grown out extensions, bonds far from the lid,

00:01:15.796 --> 00:01:18.528
and extensions turned sideways or sticking out.

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:21.168
Look for stickies, and loose extensions.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.528
Those are the ones to remove.

00:01:23.137 --> 00:01:23.987
Step four:

00:01:24.163 --> 00:01:25.987
remove the grown out extensions.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.587
Put a little cream remover on the tip of a disposable micro brush.

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:33.040
Dab it only on the bond of the extension you want to remove,

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:35.667
without touching the eyelid skin or the lash base.

00:01:35.921 --> 00:01:39.107
Wait exactly the time the maker gives, for the glue to soften.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.396
Then, with a pair of tweezers holding the natural lash still,

00:01:43.346 --> 00:01:46.874
use the other to slide the extension gently toward the tip,

00:01:46.966 --> 00:01:48.314
off the natural lash.

00:01:48.722 --> 00:01:52.394
If the extension does not slide off, the glue is not soft yet.

00:01:52.735 --> 00:01:53.514
Never pull.

00:01:53.902 --> 00:01:57.434
Dab on a little more, wait a little longer, then try again.

00:01:57.856 --> 00:02:01.731
Once it is off, wipe away any remover left on the natural lash,

00:02:01.681 --> 00:02:03.674
so the new extension bonds well.

00:02:04.353 --> 00:02:05.275
Step five:

00:02:05.456 --> 00:02:06.155
refill.

00:02:07.014 --> 00:02:09.519
On the natural lashes you have just cleared,

00:02:09.469 --> 00:02:13.035
and on new baby lashes that are long enough, isolate each lash,

00:02:13.224 --> 00:02:15.755
then attach as in the classic or volume lesson.

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:19.237
Follow the lash map recorded in the client's profile,

00:02:19.187 --> 00:02:21.115
so the set is as even as last time.

00:02:21.528 --> 00:02:25.835
Baby lashes that are still too short or too fine, leave for the next refill.

00:02:26.057 --> 00:02:31.115
And never choose longer or thicker extensions than last time just because the client wants it fuller:

00:02:31.455 --> 00:02:34.555
an extension must always suit the strength of the natural lash.

00:02:35.208 --> 00:02:35.998
Step six:

00:02:36.258 --> 00:02:38.158
check for stickies after each zone.

00:02:38.587 --> 00:02:40.558
Glide the tweezers from base to tip:

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.718
every lash must stand on its own.

00:02:43.147 --> 00:02:45.127
Then brush again, compare both eyes,

00:02:45.077 --> 00:02:48.398
and remove the pads while the client's eyes are still closed.

00:02:48.825 --> 00:02:52.341
If, during the refill, you find the set is too messy,

00:02:52.291 --> 00:02:54.958
with every lash going its own way, stop,

00:02:55.146 --> 00:02:59.038
be honest with the client, and suggest removing everything and starting fresh.

00:02:59.707 --> 00:03:00.560
Step seven:

00:03:00.727 --> 00:03:01.760
book and record.

00:03:02.154 --> 00:03:05.083
Book the next refill while the client is still sitting there,

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.640
usually after two to three weeks.

00:03:06.989 --> 00:03:10.880
Then write in the internal notes in the client's profile in VaraaAi:

00:03:11.072 --> 00:03:15.278
how the lashes held, how many you removed, the cause of shedding if any,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.720
and what advice you gave.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.440
Next time, whichever technician does the refill knows right away what to watch for.

00:03:22.049 --> 00:03:22.739
Part two:

00:03:22.938 --> 00:03:23.779
full removal.

00:03:24.061 --> 00:03:24.819
Step one:

00:03:25.248 --> 00:03:28.819
place the under eye pads carefully, covering the lower lashes.

00:03:29.132 --> 00:03:33.539
Here, the pads also protect the skin and the lower lashes from the remover.

00:03:33.887 --> 00:03:35.619
Her eyes stay fully closed.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:36.419
Tell her:

00:03:36.686 --> 00:03:39.859
if she feels stinging or heat, she should say so right away.

00:03:40.107 --> 00:03:43.705
If the client is having the lashes removed because of a reaction,

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.779
the skin around her eyes is sensitive,

00:03:45.966 --> 00:03:51.059
so work very gently, very slowly, and add no product you do not need.

00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:52.502
Step two:

00:03:52.685 --> 00:03:54.102
apply the cream remover.

00:03:54.504 --> 00:03:58.373
With a small brush, apply a thin layer of cream along the bonds,

00:03:58.323 --> 00:04:00.342
a little away from the lash base,

00:04:00.372 --> 00:04:02.342
from the inner corner to the outer corner.

00:04:02.771 --> 00:04:07.382
The cream stays on the lashes only, not on the eyelid skin, not on the waterline.

00:04:07.756 --> 00:04:09.062
Never apply too much:

00:04:09.254 --> 00:04:11.542
excess cream runs easily toward the eye.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.342
Then wait exactly the time the maker gives.

00:04:14.683 --> 00:04:18.422
While you wait, stay beside the client, and never walk away.

00:04:18.753 --> 00:04:19.702
Never rush.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:23.141
Stroke before the time is up, while the glue is still hard,

00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:25.462
and you will pull out the natural lashes too.

00:04:26.121 --> 00:04:26.911
Step three:

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:28.591
slide the lashes off.

00:04:28.844 --> 00:04:33.397
With a cotton swab or a clean small brush, stroke gently along the lashes,

00:04:33.347 --> 00:04:34.431
from base to tip.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.871
The extensions slide off, and fall onto the pad.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.311
Use a clean side for each stroke, or a fresh swab.

00:04:41.737 --> 00:04:45.391
Any extension still attached, apply more, and wait more.

00:04:45.579 --> 00:04:46.431
Never pull.

00:04:47.071 --> 00:04:47.947
Step four:

00:04:48.056 --> 00:04:48.747
cleanse.

00:04:49.231 --> 00:04:51.867
Remover left on the lashes can cause irritation.

00:04:52.146 --> 00:04:56.267
Wash the lashes thoroughly with lash cleanser, brushing from base to tip.

00:04:56.604 --> 00:04:58.907
Then rinse with clean water, and dry.

00:04:59.588 --> 00:05:00.440
Step five:

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:02.120
check the natural lashes.

00:05:02.507 --> 00:05:04.841
Any extensions left, any glue left,

00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:08.040
any broken or sparse areas in the natural lashes?

00:05:08.377 --> 00:05:11.160
Ask the client whether she feels any stinging or burning.

00:05:11.654 --> 00:05:15.080
Remove the pads gently, and let her open her eyes slowly.

00:05:15.657 --> 00:05:16.760
Tell her beforehand:

00:05:17.109 --> 00:05:20.798
natural lashes usually look sparser after removal than she remembers,

00:05:20.748 --> 00:05:21.800
and that is normal.

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.320
Then give her advice:

00:05:23.576 --> 00:05:26.920
no rubbing, oil free products, brush gently.

00:05:27.412 --> 00:05:31.820
If she had the lashes removed because of a reaction, advise her to see a doctor,

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.400
and record it in her profile.

00:05:33.926 --> 00:05:37.960
Used swabs, small brushes and pads go into a lidded bin.

00:05:38.387 --> 00:05:41.640
Tweezers are disinfected, as in the lesson on handling tools.

00:05:42.272 --> 00:05:42.916
Remember:

00:05:43.185 --> 00:05:47.316
a refill means removing the right lashes, and attaching the right lashes.

00:05:47.745 --> 00:05:53.007
A removal means remover in the right place, waiting the right time, stroking gently,

00:05:52.957 --> 00:05:53.876
never pulling.

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:56.916
And now, take the short quiz below the video.
